issue.description:
Refine the accepted Tactile treatment for surface-style Tabs so the decorative TabsList ring uses the semantic border token rather than the semantic focus ring token.

## Context

The current accepted Tactile Tabs treatment from <issue id="a39a8708-c195-4204-aea7-97a4fd2bb2cb" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-124/simplify-tactile-tabs-effect-to-a-fixed-tabslist-ring">PUI-124</issue> is:

`ring-1 ring-ring/20`

on the `TabsList` container.

That works mechanically, but the `ring` token is a focus/interaction semantic and may legitimately be chromatic in a theme, such as orange, blue, purple, or another accent color.

For this decorative container edge, that can make the TabsList look like a focus state or brand-accent treatment rather than a restrained tactile surface.

The `border` token is a safer semantic fit because it is intended for structural separation and remains more consistently subtle across themes.

## Change

When UI Effects = Tactile, surface-style Tabs should use:

`ring-1 ring-border/80`

on the `TabsList` container.

This replaces:

`ring-1 ring-ring/20`

## Semantic intent

The TabsList ring is:

* decorative;
* structural;
* part of the tactile surface treatment;
* not a focus indicator.

Therefore:

* use the semantic `border` token for the decorative TabsList ring;
* keep actual focus-visible treatments using the semantic `ring` token as currently accepted.

Do not globally replace `ring` with `border`.

## Preserve accepted UI Effects behavior

### Effect = Off

* Secondary Buttons remain flat.
* Surface-style Tabs use normal/default shadcn appearance.
* No extra TabsList ring.
* Strength remains disabled/de-emphasized.

### Effect = Tactile

* Secondary Buttons keep the existing Strength-controlled tactile treatment.
* Surface-style Tabs keep normal/default shadcn selected trigger styling.
* TabsList gets exactly:
  * `ring-1 ring-border/80`
* Tabs remain unaffected by Strength.

Line/minimal Tabs remain excluded.

## Scope

Apply only to the decorative Tactile ring on accepted surface-style `TabsList` containers.

Do not change:

* focus-visible ring semantics;
* Button tactile treatment;
* Strength mapping;
* TabsTrigger selected styling;
* tab sizing/layout;
* Theme v3 schema;
* UI Effects persisted state;
* history/reset;
* import/export;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry.

No new dependency, network behavior, or component API change.

## Verification

Verify at minimum:

* Tactile surface Tabs use `ring-1 ring-border/80`;
* Off removes the extra ring entirely;
* changing Strength does not alter Tabs;
* chromatic theme `ring` values no longer tint the decorative TabsList outline;
* actual focus-visible treatments still use the semantic `ring` token;
* light/dark modes remain coherent;
* Amber Dusk renders the TabsList edge as a restrained structural outline;
* no regression to keyboard navigation, focus visibility, selected-state semantics, or responsive layout.

## Acceptance

* Decorative Tactile TabsList ring uses `border`, not `ring`, as its color semantic.
* Final class treatment is `ring-1 ring-border/80` or the exact accepted equivalent if source architecture requires equivalent composition.
* Actual focus indicators continue using the theme's `ring` token.
* Tabs remain unaffected by Strength.
* Off/Tactile behavior otherwise remains unchanged.
* No Theme v3, schema, persistence, Design Command, mutation, registry, dependency, network, or public API regression is introduced.
